title: Victor Papanek
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Designer and teacher. Wrote //Design for the Real World// (1971).

It opens by saying there are professions more harmful than industrial design, but only a very few of them.

He wanted designers to work on what people need, with what is at hand, and to give the plans away.

See [[Design as an Attitude]], [[Enzo Mari]], [[First, the designer must determine if the project deserves to exist]], [[Sustainable Design]]
